      "blockId": "poly-cub-blk-1",
      "kind": "summary",
      "heading": "Cubic Polynomial Relations",
      "content": "For cubic $p(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d$ ($a \\ne 0$) with zeroes $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$:\n1. $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = -b/a$\n2. $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = c/a$\n3. $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -d/a$"
    }
  ],
  "workedExamples": [
    {
      "prompt": "Verify that 3, -1, -1/3 are zeroes of p(x) = 3x^3 - 5x^2 - 11x - 3.",
      "steps": [
        "Step 1: Evaluate p(3) = 3(27) - 5(9) - 11(3) - 3 = 81 - 45 - 33 - 3 = 0.",
        "Step 2: Evaluate p(-1) = 3(-1) - 5(1) - 11(-1) - 3 = -3 - 5 + 11 - 3 = 0.",
        "Step 3: Evaluate p(-1/3) = 0.",
        "Step 4: Sum of zeroes = 3 - 1 - 1/3 = 5/3. -b/a = -(-5)/3 = 5/3."
      ],
      "answer": "Verified"
    }
  ],
